                <note rend="inline" type="source">825.6362/33: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Chile</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Hofer</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-11-16T12:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 16,
                                1927—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received 5:50 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>176. Ambassador’s telegram 168, November 2, 4 p.m. Chamber of Deputies passed
                    coal bill substantially as reported by joint committee late yesterday after
                    short discussion. Bill expected to be sent promptly to the Senate.</p>
                <p>[Paraphrase.] Seibert says that there is little hope for effective modifications
                    since prestige of Government and Minister of Finance, who has suffered much
                    embarrassment by protests, is involved if Congress does not promptly approve
                    bill. [End paraphrase.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hofer</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
